  "title": "Preserve broadcasting in CanonicalStiefel retraction and transport",
  "body": "## Problem\n\n`CanonicalStiefel.retr_transp` fails for valid broadcastable point, step, and tangent-vector batches. For example, a single point and tangent vector with a batch of retraction steps reaches the linear solve, then crashes because its result is reshaped using the original point shape. Broadcasting the point or transported vectors instead can fail earlier in `torch.cat`. The same issue affects `expmap_transp`, `ManifoldTensor` delegation, and scaled manifolds.\n\nThe separate retraction and transport methods already accept these inputs.\n\n## Change\n\nBroadcast the point and step before the joint solve, broadcast the transported vectors when they fit that point batch, and split the result using its actual output shape. When the vectors introduce additional batch axes, use the separate public methods so those axes expand only the transported-vector result. The point output continues to depend only on the point and step, including when the extra vector axis has size one.\n\nThe existing one-solve path remains for matching batches and for broadcasts that do not enlarge the point batch.\n\n## Validation\n\nThe regressions compare joint results with explicit loops over the separate public retraction and transport methods. They also check point orthogonality, tangent constraints, canonical metric preservation, gradients back to broadcast inputs, noncontiguous inputs, empty batches, the `expmap_transp` alias, `ManifoldTensor`, and `Scaled`.\n\nOn both Python 3.8 / PyTorch 2.0.1 CPU and Python 3.12 / PyTorch 2.8.0 CPU:\n\n- The unchanged implementation produces **34 failures and 8 passing controls**, without collection errors or skips.\n- All **42 new cases** pass with the fix. The complete regression, canonical-projection, manifold-basic, Riemannian-SGD, Adam, scaling, tensor-API, and retraction-derivative modules report **2243 passed, 310 existing skips**.\n- Production and regression Ruff checks, `git diff --check`, and the clean-source check pass.\n\n[Baseline and fixed CI results](https://github.com/Afloat16/geoopt/actions/runs/43672475302). The verification workflow is on a separate fork branch.\n",
  "prefilled_url": "https://github.com/geoopt/geoopt/compare/master...Afloat16:fix/canonical-stiefel-broadcast-transport-20261115?expand=1&title=Preserve%20broadcasting%20in%20CanonicalStiefel%20retraction%20and%20transport&body=%23%23%20Problem%0A%0A%60CanonicalStiefel.retr_transp%60%20fails%20for%20valid%20broadcastable%20point%2C%20step%2C%20and%20tangent-vector%20batches.%20For%20example%2C%20a%20single%20point%20and%20tangent%20vector%20with%20a%20batch%20of%20retraction%20steps%20reaches%20the%20linear%20solve%2C%20then%20crashes%20because%20its%20result%20is%20reshaped%20using%20the%20original%20point%20shape.%20Broadcasting%20the%20point%20or%20transported%20vectors%20instead%20can%20fail%20earlier%20in%20%60torch.cat%60.%20The%20same%20issue%20affects%20%60expmap_transp%60%2C%20%60ManifoldTensor%60%20delegation%2C%20and%20scaled%20manifolds.%0A%0AThe%20separate%20retraction%20and%20transport%20methods%20already%20accept%20these%20inputs.%0A%0A%23%23%20Change%0A%0ABroadcast%20the%20point%20and%20step%20before%20the%20joint%20solve%2C%20broadcast%20the%20transported%20vectors%20when%20they%20fit%20that%20point%20batch%2C%20and%20split%20the%20result%20using%20its%20actual%20output%20shape.%20When%20the%20vectors%20introduce%20additional%20batch%20axes%2C%20use%20the%20separate%20public%20methods%20so%20those%20axes%20expand%20only%20the%20transported-vector%20result.%20The%20point%20output%20continues%20to%20depend%20only%20on%20the%20point%20and%20step%2C%20including%20when%20the%20extra%20vector%20axis%20has%20size%20one.%0A%0AThe%20existing%20one-solve%20path%20remains%20for%20matching%20batches%20and%20for%20broadcasts%20that%20do%20not%20enlarge%20the%20point%20batch.%0A%0A%23%23%20Validation%0A%0AThe%20regressions%20compare%20joint%20results%20with%20explicit%20loops%20over%20the%20separate%20public%20retraction%20and%20transport%20methods.%20They%20also%20check%20point%20orthogonality%2C%20tangent%20constraints%2C%20canonical%20metric%20preservation%2C%20gradients%20back%20to%20broadcast%20inputs%2C%20noncontiguous%20inputs%2C%20empty%20batches%2C%20the%20%60expmap_transp%60%20alias%2C%20%60ManifoldTensor%60%2C%20and%20%60Scaled%60.%0A%0AOn%20both%20Python%203.8%20%2F%20PyTorch%202.0.1%20CPU%20and%20Python%203.12%20%2F%20PyTorch%202.8.0%20CPU%3A%0A%0A-%20The%20unchanged%20implementation%20produces%20**34%20failures%20and%208%20passing%20controls**%2C%20without%20collection%20errors%20or%20skips.%0A-%20All%20**42%20new%20cases**%20pass%20with%20the%20fix.%20The%20complete%20regression%2C%20canonical-projection%2C%20manifold-basic%2C%20Riemannian-SGD%2C%20Adam%2C%20scaling%2C%20tensor-API%2C%20and%20retraction-derivative%20modules%20report%20**2243%20passed%2C%20310%20existing%20skips**.%0A-%20Production%20and%20regression%20Ruff%20checks%2C%20%60git%20diff%20--check%60%2C%20and%20the%20clean-source%20check%20pass.%0A%0A%5BBaseline%20and%20fixed%20CI%20results%5D(https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2FAfloat16%2Fgeoopt%2Factions%2Fruns%2F43672475302).%20The%20verification%20workflow%20is%20on%20a%20separate%20fork%20branch.%0A",
